      const params = new URLSearchParams(location.search);
      const tab    = params.get('tab') ?? 'inbox';
      params.delete('tab');
      const target = TAB_TO_ROUTE[tab] ?? '/notifications/inbox';
      const to     = qs ? `${target}?${qs}` : target;
      return <Navigate to={to} replace />;
  Native mapping (one-for-one):
    - useLocation()              -> LegacyNotificationsRedirectSource (P1/S8 seam; no HTTP in view)
    - URLSearchParams(search)    -> Resolver.parseQuery (ordered URLQueryItem, leading '?' tolerated)
    - params.get('tab') ?? inbox -> NotificationsRedirectTab(tabParameter:) — first `tab`, missing→inbox
    - params.delete('tab')       -> forwardedItems = items.filter { name != "tab" } (drops EVERY entry)
    - TAB_TO_ROUTE[tab] ?? inbox -> NotificationsRedirectTab paths + unknown-string→inbox (usedFallback)
    - qs ? target?qs : target    -> ResolvedRedirect.target (bare path when nothing forwarded)
    - <Navigate to replace/>     -> LegacyNotificationsRedirectRouter.replace(with:) dispatched ONCE on mount
  TAB_TO_ROUTE parity asserted: inbox→/notifications/inbox, archived→/notifications/archived,
    channels→/notifications/channels; fallback /notifications/inbox.

=== STATES (every state renders — never a blank box) ===
  The web spec's generic state list maps onto a SYNCHRONOUS redirect (useLocation is
  router state, not a network resource — there is no loading/error/stale/offline data
  envelope). Reproduced honestly:
    - resolving  : transient redirect affordance (ProgressView + label) — the native
                   stand-in for the web's invisible/instant <Navigate>. (= "loading")
